message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EIT-SP: Educational Interactive Toolkit for Semiconductor Physics"
abbreviation: "EIT-SP"
abstract: >-
  A growing series of single-file, zero-dependency interactive HTML tools for teaching and
  learning semiconductor physics. Tools are added as they mature; those not yet ready are
  not published, so the collection expands over time. It is organised according to the
  chapter sequence of a standard
  Chinese semiconductor-physics textbook: crystal structure and energy bands,
  impurities and defects, carrier statistics, electrical conductivity,
  non-equilibrium carriers, pn junctions, semiconductor surfaces and MIS
  structures, and optical, thermoelectric and magnetic effects.
  Each tool is a self-contained HTML file with no build step, no external
  libraries and no network requests, so it runs offline and remains usable
  without maintenance.
